    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## \u2713 Fixed!\n\nThe bug was a floating-point precision issue in the `parseEuros` function. When converting \"39.95\" to cents, the code was doing:\n```javascript\nNumber(39.95).toFixed(2) * 100  // \u2192 3995.0000000000005\n```\n\nThe fix avoids floating-point arithmetic entirely by parsing the string directly into integer cents:\n```javascript\n// \"39.95\" \u2192 euros=39, cents=95 \u2192 3900 + 95 = 3995 (exact)\nconst euros = parseInt(parts[0], 10);\nconst cents = parts[1] ? parseInt(parts[1].padEnd(2, '0'), 10) : 0;\nreturn euros * 100 + cents;\n```\n\n**Verified:**\n- \u2705 All 50 existing tests pass\n- \u2705 New test for 39.95 passes\n- \u2705 CLI command works: `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03` \u2192 Gym is stored correctly\n- \u2705 Netflix (12.99) and Spotify (10.99) still work as before",
